+Why: The fix joins quoted continuation lines, but it still splits on \n, so CRLF input keeps a trailing \r on every line. Because the closing quote is followed by \r, strip('"') cannot remove it. The issue's repro returns 3 rows, but Ben's note is `call back\r\nafter 5pm"\r` instead of `call back\r\nafter 5pm`; the header and Ana fields also keep stray \r and quote characters. The new test's first assertion would fail on main, but it uses LF-only input, so it passes while the reported CRLF case stays broken; its second assertion also wrongly expects a quoted comma to split fields.
